# Security AppSec (Auto — WordPress plugin)

## Precedence
Defers to `.cursorrules` Safety. Deeper stack detail: `docs/standards/php-wordpress.md` §9, and the `wp-plugin-development` skill.

## Secrets
- Never hardcode credentials, API keys, tokens, licence keys, or connection strings
- Never commit `wp-config.php`, `.env`, or client site credentials
- Never log passwords, tokens, session IDs, or a full `$_POST` / webhook body

## PHP entry guard
- Every PHP file starts with `if (!defined('ABSPATH')) { exit; }`
- No new global functions without the `twork_` prefix; options/transients/meta keys prefixed too

## Output escaping (render callbacks + templates)
| Context | Function |
|---|---|
| HTML text | `esc_html()` |
| Attribute | `esc_attr()` |
| URL | `esc_url()` |
| Inside `<script>` | `wp_json_encode()` |
| Rich text / block content | `wp_kses_post()` |
- Escape **at output**, every time — including block attributes coming from the editor
- `printf` with placeholders over string concatenation

## Input
- Sanitize on input: `sanitize_text_field`, `sanitize_email`, `absint`, `esc_url_raw`, `wp_kses_post`
- Allow-list enum-style attributes (layout, variant, columns) instead of trusting the saved value
- `$wpdb->prepare()` on every custom query; never interpolate into `$wpdb->query()`

## AuthZ / CSRF
- `current_user_can()` on every admin action, AJAX handler, and REST callback
- Nonce verification on every form and AJAX call (`check_admin_referer` / `wp_verify_nonce`)
- Real `permission_callback` on `register_rest_route()` — `__return_true` only for genuinely public data
- `is_admin()` is not a permission check

## JS
- No `eval`; no `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` / `innerHTML` with unsanitized user or attribute data
- Prefer `RawHTML` with server-sanitized content, or `textContent` in front-end scripts
- Localize data with `wp_localize_script` / `wp_add_inline_script` + `wp_json_encode` — never inject raw PHP into a script tag

## Dangerous PHP
- Never `eval()`, `extract()`, `create_function()`, or `unserialize()` on user data
- `hash_equals()` for secret comparison; `wp_generate_password()` / `random_bytes()` for tokens

## Dependencies
- Do not add packages without need + approval path; confirm the package exists before install
- Prefer WordPress core APIs and existing in-tree helpers over new libraries

## PII
- Booking/contact form entries, patient-facing enquiries, and doctor data are personal data
- No PII in front-end globals, HTML comments, or logs; log IDs, not emails

## Do not
- Weaken security “to make it sound less serious”
- Touch production secrets or paste client credentials into replies
- Disable escaping to “fix” a rendering bug
